{%- set data = CTX.calendar|d or (templates('${UUID}') | from_json_string) -%}

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
</head>
<body>
        <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        }
        .myTable {
            border-collapse: collapse;
            width: 100%;
        }
        .myTable th, .myTable td {
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            padding: 8px;
            text-align: left;
        }
        .myTable th {
            background-color: #009490;
            color: white;
        }
        .myTable .goal-col {
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        .myTable tr:nth-child(even) {
            background-color: #B2DFD8;
        }
    </style>
    <p>
    Greetings, and welcome to the Rewst community! As a new Training Programniversity Freshman, we're egg-cited to accompany you on your journey to success. Our team has put together the following plan to help navigate your initial training and development. And remember, should you have any questions or need support, don't hesitate to give us a squawk. We're here to ensure your transition into our community is as smooth as possible. Let's get this journey started!
    </p>
    <p>
    For the 100 series, we have courses numbered 101 through 106. These ideally should be taken in order, especially 102-106, as these start you out building a simple workflow, and then make it better through iteration.
    </p>
    <p>
    This content is self-paced. We offer courses sequentially, but if your schedule doesn't allow you to attend consecutive days, you can always re-schedule for the next offered session. If you follow the schedule below, you should be able to complete 100-level training and certification within one month. We recommend you attend the live sessions and ask questions if you can, but in case the times don't work out for you, we have recorded sessions ready to watch.
    </p>
    <p>
    Use the hyperlinks in the calendar view to sign up for each event, and let us know if you need any help along the way!
    <br><br><br>
    <table class="myTable">
        <tr>
            <th>Week</th>
            <th class="goal-col">Goals of the Week</th>
            <th>Monday</th>
            <th>Tuesday</th>
            <th>Wednesday</th>
            <th>Thursday</th>
            <th>Friday</th>
        </tr>
        {% for week in data.weeks %}
            <tr>
                <td>{{week.week_name}}</td>
                <td class="goal-col">
                    <ul>
                    {% for goal in week.weekly_goals %}
                        <li>{{goal}}</li>
                    {% endfor %}
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td>{% for item in week.monday %}{{item}}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
                <td>{% for item in week.tuesday %}{{item}}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
                <td>{% for item in week.wednesday %}{{item}}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
                <td>{% for item in week.thursday %}{{item}}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
                <td>{% for item in week.friday %}{{item}}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
            </tr>
        {% endfor %}
    </table>
</body>
</html>

